# I04.var09 independent prospective contract review — GO_CONTRACT_ONLY

**Decision:** `GO_CONTRACT_ONLY` for the proposed read-only classification of the already accepted I04.var03 v1.0.1 run. This permits construction of a distinct classification package and independent reader. It authorizes no new model, SSH preflight, native run, accepted checker rerun, catalog append, or publication.

The reviewed prospective contract is `tmp/i04-var09-prospective-v100-20261008-01/contract.json` (13,997 bytes; SHA-256 `ec2dbe37601d0045185109fe7856ea4656a0b2e01dfe35ac25809de17aa60307`), with companion `contract.md` (5,689 bytes; SHA-256 `9d8a5047c8e8f090b090b0307553cead51a665813525a6d4f2ca2c053ba085de`). It declares classification ID `i04-var09-arrived-system-next-mission-v100-20261008-01`, distinct from unchanged accepted native run ID `i04-var03-idle-system-between-v101-ssh-20261008-01`.

The independent read-only audit method `tmp/i04-var09-independent-contract-audit-v100-20261008.py` is 9,794 bytes/SHA-256 `574d48c8e28573b1073220c46b0fb1f92cdf20d216a8b65327660eeb7aab8779`. Root's original binary capture `tmp/i04-var09-root-review-proofs-v100-20261008/independent-contract-20261008T112723518374Z-4882b788/receipt.json` is 1,367 bytes/SHA-256 `0c52f59ddbdf78bc9b2c7c674f4457d183eeaa588f94bcb0bfc70096c0861ae7`: actual integer exit 0, empty original stderr, 115-byte original stdout/SHA-256 `5d51d32c3a30e11032ac7472e7fdc9b062c5a5856e12d4e2f9132331e19934a3`, unchanged capture and reviewer method hashes, and no native dispatch. The method rehashed the 401 accepted indexed sources, 153 raw plus 15 separate preflight originals, 456 parent prelaunch roles with consistent repeated-path pins, prior independent GO, input/log/report/closure originals, and distinct historical catalog local/Git archives. It checked the source transfer row, the 118-line/104-timed original log and observed ID0 chain, and ten declared selected report cells. Root's separate eligibility receipt `tmp/i04-var09-root-selection-20261008/20261008T111751488105Z-e0b84a11/receipt.json` (9,507 bytes/SHA-256 `f198bdf3ef4e4778ac2dca5d87d185afb74b94f214aeebf5da4cef800a156192`) covers 403 current disk/Git pair roles, installed pins, current catalog498 and absent classification paths.

The supported claim is only the task side of the catalog's OR branch: original numeric aircraft ID `<TEACH-AIR-01,0>` leaves TEACH-UNIT at h10.5, enters and becomes ready at TEACH-UNIT-2 at h11, is allocated to a later mission at h19, launches h20, performs its task h20.5–21.5, completes the mission and returns ready at the target h22. The original source has one transfer row, and the log has one transfer out/in. There is no observed second or reverse transfer, general system identity or transfer priority claim, or new native behavior result. The previously accepted independent full 4,044-cell report GO is rehashed as provenance; the new classification may add separate selected-cell assertions but must not claim a fresh full-report acceptance. This scope correction is frozen in `tmp/i04-var09-independent-reuse-feasibility-addendum-20261008.md` (1,377 bytes/SHA-256 `51c80c60e26cbe16460a74ce062368f6f3554fc3837573d81101023d3ec9189c`).

Before any classification acceptance, the new independent reader must parse every original log line and continuation with a closed grammar, accumulate per-ID source/transit/target ownership and ready/mission/task states, and run in-memory negative clones that call its semantic ledger directly, separated from the outer original SHA gate. It must check typed selected report cells while retaining the prior full-report verdict as a separate provenance record. Sealed custody must preserve the accepted parent manifest's historical 496-entry live-catalog alias through its exact archive, current 498-entry catalog identity, and distinct CRLF/LF bytes; the two private unrelated-app originals stay mandatory local evidence and are not published. Subsequent method, captured classification, content, catalog, staged, and remote decisions remain independent gates.
